 terms and to test whether a number belongs to a pattern","attempts":2,"unaidedCorrect":0}],"misconceptions":[{"belief":"Thinks doubling the step number doubles the term (if step 10 has 31, step 20 has 62)","timesSeen":1,"correctAfterLastSeen":0}]}},"start":{"ms":2879,"topic":{"id":"c7-maths-ch04-t03","title":"Patterns and relationships with algebra","chapter":"Expressions using Letter-Numbers"},"teacher":"Asha","address":"aap"},"lessonId":"29f9fd4d-4d8d-49bb-840c-6d7ec1a6b046","boardPages":[{"seq":1,"intentId":"29f9fd4d-4d8d-49bb-840c-6d7ec1a6b046:wb:3","beat":"explain","skillId":"c7-maths-ch04-t03-s1","at":"2026-10-21T14:59:39.264Z","board":"drawing with 2 arrow; written: \"3n + ?\" \"every step\" \"100th step\" \"amount added\" \"multiplier of n\" \"fixed number\" \"step ?\""},{"seq":2,"intentId":"29f9fd4d-4d8d-49bb-840c-6d7ec1a6b046:wb:4","beat":"worked_example","skillId":"c7-maths-ch04-t03-s1","at":"2026-10-21T14:59:45.612Z","board":"drawing with 5 rect, 4 arrow; written: \"Each step\" \"adds 3\" \"The rule\" \"has 3n\" \"Add ? to\" \"match step ?\" \"Check n = ?\" \"30th term\" \"is 92\""},{"seq":3,"intentId":"29f9fd4d-4d8d-49bb-840c-6d7ec1a6b046:wb:8","beat":"explain","skillId":"c7-maths-ch04-t03-s2","at":"2026-10-21T15:00:03.902Z","board":"drawing with 4 circle, 4 arrow; written: \"pattern\" \"rule\""},{"seq":4,"intentId":"29f9fd4d-4d8d-49bb-840c-6d7ec1a6b046:wb:13","beat":"contrast","skillId":"c7-maths-ch04-t03-s2","at":"2026-10-21T15:00:32.991Z","board":"drawing with 1 circle; written: \"Step ?\" \"31 dots\" \"?n + ?\" \"Step 20\" \"? dots\" \"Check: ? × 20 + ?\""}],"lane2":{"teacher":"director","agent":null},"finishedAt":"2026-10-21T15:00:46.293Z","arm":"director"}